venue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Shake Shack, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $3.2B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $57M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.86\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 29\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 105% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.0493505698547265},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"